      "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
      "description": "Check that `AtomicMass.lean` is still in sync with the data table it is generated from. THE SMALLEST WORKFLOW HERE, AND THE ONE WHOSE OUTPUT A PROOF DEPENDS ON. `AtomicMass.lean` is generated from a data table; if the two part company, a Lean file that compiles is nevertheless carrying numbers nothing produced. So the job regenerates and diffs, and any difference is red.\n\nThe check itself is the shared `generated-file-drift` process (Process_GeneratedFileDrift), drawn once for every drift check. This diagram stays because its workflow's job names Start_Change (`# bpmn-node:`), which is what lets check:workflow-coverage see the job.",
