    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-sci/process/Process_PaperAuthoring",
      "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
      "description": "How a scientific paper or book folio is authored end to end, with Lean for its formal claims and LaTeX for its typesetting. folio-assistant — authoring a scientific paper end to end (Lean + LaTeX).\nSource of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other\nBPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it\nby `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.\nThe <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill\nthat implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared\nwork plan in beans/.\n\nReview, publish and committee feedback are core's shared Process_FolioReviewPublish, called after rendering (shared block G6 of the BPMN guidance review, owner Q-BR-7 A, 2026-11-01). Its `no` answer, changes asked, comes back to Task_AuthorBlocks.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 17,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-sci/directory/sci-processes",
      "name": "Authoring a paper",
      "nodeCount": 16,
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn",
